  "body": "[PR #1038](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1038) evaluates Machin and Taylor series at every data site. This package\nreplaces that phase interface with two reversible dyadic phase states.\nIt uses a fixed second difference, bounded three-shear rotations, and\n`Q=W+2 bit_length(L+1)+20` state bits. Every pass reconstructs its phase\nstate backward. Seed and chart coefficients clear exactly. No phase\narray or checkpoint list is stored.\n\nReview files: [Proof and scope](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/1627bf208f80e490522343590dd52f38b329e238/research/dirty-stride-fast-phases/PROOF.md) \u00b7 [Evidence](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/1627bf208f80e490522343590dd52f38b329e238/research/dirty-stride-fast-phases/VALIDATION.md) \u00b7 [Source pins and credit](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/1627bf208f80e490522343590dd52f38b329e238/research/dirty-stride-fast-phases/SOURCE.json).\n\nThe proof gives a uniform quadratic drift bound and the same emitted\ncoefficient accuracy as [PR #1038](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1038). The retained dirty wrappers therefore\nkeep their large-target error bound, exact source and borrowed-array\nrestoration, original precision, and two-data-tape movement bill. One\nprepared phase object serves all four passes of a complete dirty word.\nIts stream uses `60L+6` real products and `24L` chart divisions. Exact\nseed preparation and erasure add `O(P)` scalar operations on wider\nrational operands, where `P=Q+24`.\n\nStatus: enabling construction. The elementary phase bit bound is\n`O((A+V)^2+P S^2+L T^2)`, where `A` is the original numerator width,\n`V` is the modulus width, `S=16(P+V+1)^2`, and `T` covers stream and\ndata widths. A direct reversible arithmetic compiler needs\n`O((A+V)^2+S^2+T^2)` clean scratch bits. The Python reference implements\nthe scalar state and exact series cleanup; it does not emit a native\nbit-gate program. No new kappa is claimed.\n\nThe base is [abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf). [PR #1038](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1038) is pinned\nat [99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9); nine retained files have\nGit-blob and SHA256 pins. No moving selected-result file is source-pinned.\n[PR #1054](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1054) and [PR #1025](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1025) are scope references, not combined theorems. The\ninherited logarithmic borrowed-array pool stays fixed. Supplier hosting,\nfactor production, multi-axis composition, and outer assembly stay open.\n\nVerification:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/dirty-stride-fast-phases/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/dirty-stride-fast-phases/test_package.py\n```\n\nThe main receipt covers 98 phase cases, 1,474 rational interval samples,\n16 dirty words, three same-input work comparisons, and seven input or\nlifecycle controls. It executes and reverses all 16,384 steps of the\nlong case. The package check rejects seven semantic faults and source\ncorruption, then replays the full receipt from read-only relocated files.\nIt returned 0 in 245.149 seconds. The parent agent also completed the\noptimized main replay. These checks are finite evidence for the written\nproof, not independent human review or formal multiplication verification.\n\nTiming results are mixed. Three alternating same-input trials give\n[PR #1038](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1038)/new median seconds of `0.042217/0.191425` at `(L,W)=(32,16)`,\n`0.689942/1.286691` at `(257,48)`, and `10.187936/9.092779` at\n`(2048,96)`. New seed erasure is included. Seed operands reach 55,767\nbits in the last case. All final trials and an earlier run's medians\nare disclosed. The shared-host timings do not establish a general\nspeedup. The result is the proved interface and its separate work bill.\n\n[NOTICE.md](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/1627bf208f80e490522343590dd52f38b329e238/research/dirty-stride-fast-phases/NOTICE.md) preserves predecessor credit and discloses substantial OpenAI\nCodex assistance. New material is by Ali Romman (@aliromman) under Apache-2.0.\n[upstream/](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/1627bf208f80e490522343590dd52f38b329e238/upstream), selected certificates, and the research ledger are unchanged.\n",
